# The app's own folder: the database (PGlite, migrated at every start), the files
# (avatars, assets, attachments, imports) and the install's secret. Relative to
# apps/plot; unset is apps/plot/data/app. One process at a time: the app locks it.
# SHIZUE_DATA_DIR=./data/app
# The web app's origin (scheme://host[:port], no path). Writes must come from it
# and the ChatGPT connection returns to it. The name is kept from the earlier
# auth library. The web app reads it too: an https origin gets HSTS when the app
# is built.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:13000
# Seals the ChatGPT tokens in the database and derives this install's OpenAI
# host ID. Leave it unset: the install makes its own once, as `secret` in the
# app's folder. One set here must have at least 32 characters under
# NODE_ENV=production or a web origin that is not this machine's (openssl rand
# -base64 32). Changing it disconnects ChatGPT.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
API_PORT=8787
# Where the API listens. Loopback when it runs beside the web app; 0.0.0.0 when
# it runs on a server of its own (point the web app's API_ORIGIN at it).
# API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# How the API's log reads: text (the default) is the console as a terminal shows
# it; json, for production, makes every line one JSON object
# {time, level, msg, component?, requestId?, err?} and adds an access line per
# request.
# LOG_FORMAT=text
# Prometheus metrics on a listener of their own, never under /api. Unset is off.
# METRICS_HOST stays on loopback unless the scraper runs on another machine.
# `embedder:serve` reads them too; give it a port of its own beside an API.
# METRICS_PORT=9464
# METRICS_HOST=127.0.0.1
# How long a shutdown waits for background work the turns started (summaries,
# vectors) after it has stopped the open replies, in ms.
# SHUTDOWN_BACKGROUND_MS=20000
# The app's files are in its folder, never in S3. Only `embedder:fetch` and
# `embedder:publish` read these: KURE-v1's weights live in this bucket under models/.
S3_BUCKET=shizue-media
S3_REGION=us-east-1
# The service endpoint. Leave empty on real AWS S3 — the SDK picks the regional one.
S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:19000
# Leave both empty on AWS to use the SDK's provider chain (instance role, AWS_*).
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=shizue
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=shizue-secret
# bucket/key in the path instead of bucket. in the hostname. A local store needs it
# (a virtual-hosted bucket cannot resolve as a subdomain of localhost); AWS does not.
S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
# File imports this API process reads at once, each on a job loop of its own:
# what bounds the memory imports take (a few 8MB parts and a card's text each).
# IMPORT_WORKERS=2
# There are no accounts: a browser on this computer is the app's owner. ChatGPT,
# connected in Settings, is the AI; no API key is used. OpenAI returns to
# http://127.0.0.1:<this port>/auth/callback, and the Shizue extension (Chrome Web
# Store, 0.3.6+) rewrites that to http://localhost:13000/api/chatgpt/callback.
# Unset is 47801, the port Shizue's rule catches; set another only for an offset
# dev server with a stand-in for Shizue.
# CHATGPT_CALLBACK_PORT=47801
# A phone: Settings → Connect a phone opens a tunnel itself (Tailscale Serve, else
# a Cloudflare Quick Tunnel) and needs nothing here. A tunnel you run yourself is
# listed here instead, comma-separated (e.g. https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net:8444).
# Writes may come from them as from BETTER_AUTH_URL, which stays the origin the
# ChatGPT connection returns to and must be a loopback one; a request through one
# is the owner's only with the device session a QR code from settings pairs a
# phone with. scripts/dev.sh hands this line to `next dev` too, which otherwise
# refuses the host.
# REMOTE_ORIGINS=
# The embedding models the API runs for everything it searches by meaning, and
# where their weights are: `pnpm --filter @shizue/api embedder:fetch` puts them
# there (bge-m3 from Hugging Face, KURE-v1 from the S3 bucket above); the server
# only reads them.
# EMBEDDER_ROUTING picks a plot's model: single (the default: EMBEDDER_MODEL for
# every plot, KURE-v1 unless set — multiMiniLM is the light one for development)
# or by-language (Korean plots KURE-v1, the rest bge-m3). EMBEDDER=off runs without
# one, and so without every search by meaning: the memory's similar summaries (recent
# and random ones take their share), the facts (none are extracted or sent), chat
# retrieval, explore's search by meaning (the text search answers) and the embedding
# emotion picker (the auxiliary model picks).
# EMBEDDER_THREADS caps each model's onnxruntime threads (default: every core).
# EMBEDDER_ROUTING=single
# EMBEDDER_MODEL=KURE-v1
# EMBEDDER_CACHE_DIR=./data/embedder
# EMBEDDER_THREADS=4
# EMBEDDER=off
# Several API instances can share one embedder instead of each loading the model
# (about 2 GB, up to 3.9 GB while it embeds): run `pnpm --filter @shizue/api
# embedder:serve` (built: `node dist/embedderServe.js`) where the weights are, with
# EMBEDDER_PORT, and set EMBEDDER_URL on the instances to that address. Both sides
# read the same EMBEDDER_ROUTING and EMBEDDER_MODEL. The port is never under /api;
# off loopback (EMBEDDER_HOST) it needs EMBEDDER_TOKEN, the same on both sides. An
# API instance that sets EMBEDDER_PORT without EMBEDDER_URL serves its own model.
# EMBEDDER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8790
# EMBEDDER_PORT=8790
# EMBEDDER_HOST=127.0.0.1
# EMBEDDER_TOKEN=
# Korean aliases for the lore of works in other languages, written by the
# creator's (or the reader's) auxiliary model after an import or an edit, so a
# Korean reader's turns still reach an English book's entries. off turns the
# pass and the aliases off: those books go back to their own keys.
# LORE_ALIASES=off
# Echo is available only to automated tests running the API with NODE_ENV=test.
